   "claim": "All 63 frozen items appear verbatim, but the wave decision 'The default bind address is IPv4 127.0.0.1' says the adapter does not call InetAddress.getLoopbackAddress(), while the frozen D-211 text says it SHALL bind to InetAddress.getLoopbackAddress(). The section intro says the decisions 'add no new requirement', yet this one replaces D-211's mechanism. The loopback intent is kept and the round 4 W2-001 Android ::1 reason is sound, so this is not a correctness problem. The risk is traceability: an SRS AC or a promotion check written from the frozen D-211 text would conflict with the implementation.",
   "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-5/design.md:58 (D-211) vs the Wave decisions bullet 'The default bind address is IPv4 127.0.0.1'; docs/research/naruserve-v1/design/00.design.md:366",
   "suggested_fix": "In the wave 5 SRS, word the D-211 acceptance criterion as 'binds the IPv4 loopback 127.0.0.1 explicitly by default' and cite the wave decision as the reading of D-211, so verification evidence matches the frozen intent (loopback by default, passed explicitly) rather than the literal API call."
